Using De Moivre's theorem, we can simplify the expression as follows:

$\left(-2 (\cos (2)+i \sin (2))\right)^5$

$= (-2)^5 (\cos (2)+i \sin (2))^5$

$= -32 (\cos (2)+i \sin (2))^5$

$= -32 (\cos (5)+i \sin (5))$

Therefore, the simplified expression is $-32 (\cos (10)+i \sin (10))$.
####
The answer is $-32 (\cos (10)+i \sin (10))$

